package commands

import (
	"os"
	"path/filepath"

	"github.com/spf13/cobra"
	"github.com/spf13/cobra/doc"
)

// skillsConfig describes the agent skill generated by `genskills`.
var skillsConfig = doc.SkillsConfig{
	Name:        "suprsend-cli",
	Description: "SuprSend CLI tool for managing SuprSend account and resources from the command line — workspaces, workflows, templates, categories, events, schemas, and translations. Use ONLY when the user wants the agent to RUN a `suprsend ...` command (e.g. \"push my template\", \"pull all workflows\", \"sync staging to prod\", \"generate Python types\") or asks about a specific CLI command's flags/behavior (\"what does `suprsend template commit --dry-run` do?\"). Do NOT load for documentation, lookup, or conceptual SuprSend questions (\"how does batching work\", \"what is a variant\", \"explain delivery nodes\") — load `suprsend-docs-support` for those. Do NOT load when the user is authoring workflow or template JSON without invoking the CLI — load `suprsend-workflow-schema` or `suprsend-template-schema` for those.",
	Metadata: map[string]string{
		"author":   "suprsend",
		"category": "cli",
	},
	Notes: []string{
		"`list` commands default to `-o pretty` (a human-friendly table) and also accept `-o json` and `-o yaml`. `workflow get`, `schema get`, `event get` and `translation get` default to `-o json`, accept `-o yaml`, and reject `-o pretty`; `template get` defaults to `-o json` and also accepts `yaml` and `pretty`. `list` commands return every item unless `--limit` is given; when `--limit` leaves items out, a note on stderr gives the total and the next `--offset` (`-o json` stays a plain array).",
		"`push`, `pull`, `commit`, `enable`, `disable`, `sync` and `generate-types` always print their result on stdout, whether or not it is a terminal: a header naming the workspace, host and profile, one line per item with its status, any warnings, and a summary. Statuses: `created` / `updated` (saved as draft; push first compares each item with the workspace's draft and sends only what differs), `pushed` (saved as draft; `sync`, which doesn't compare), `committed` (live), `unchanged` (nothing differed from the workspace's draft so nothing was sent, or with a commit the draft already matched live), `skipped` (changed in the workspace since the last pull or push and not locally, so not sent), `pulled`, `would-push` / `would-commit` (dry run), `failed`. With `-o json` the result is one JSON object with `command`, `workspace`, `host`, `profile`, `dry_run`, `ok`, `counts`, `items` and `warnings`.",
		"When stderr is not a terminal (piped, as in most agent and CI shells) or with `-o json`, log lines are hidden (pass `-v info` to see them; warnings still appear in the result) and an error is one JSON object on stderr with `error`, `code` and `hint`. When a run over several items fails, the error lists each failed item and its reason, also as `details.failures`.",
		"Exit codes: 0 success; 1 API error (including a definition the API rejects as invalid on commit, code `api-validation-failed`), or any failed item in a run over several items; 2 a check the CLI runs before calling the API (unreadable file, invalid JSON or JSON Schema), also for a run over several items whose failures were all such checks; 3 auth; 4 not found (a resource or the workspace); 5 rate limited; 64 invalid usage. A command on a single resource exits with that resource's code. `-q` hides info and warning lines, never the result.",
		"Workspace: `-w` beats `SUPRSEND_WORKSPACE`, which beats the active profile's `workspace`; the fallback is `staging`. Write commands warn when they fall back to `staging`, and check that the workspace exists before writing (a typo fails with `unknown workspace` and a did-you-mean hint, exit 4). Set `SUPRSEND_REQUIRE_WORKSPACE=1` to make that fallback an error for writes (and to make `sync` require `--from` and `--to`). Run `suprsend whoami --check` to see the profile, host and workspace commands will use. The profile comes from `--profile`, else `SUPRSEND_PROFILE`, else the config file's active profile (`profile use`), so a project can pin its own profile without switching everyone's. The service token comes from `--service-token`, else `SUPRSEND_SERVICE_TOKEN`, else the profile. An invalid-token error names the host and where it and the token came from: a token only works on the host it was issued for.",
		"On `push`, `commit`, `enable` and `disable`, `--dry-run` never calls the API. `push` reads and parses the local files (schemas also get a local JSON Schema compile; `category push` parses `categories.json` but only lists the translation files); `commit`, `enable` and `disable` read nothing. They only report what would happen, and the workspace isn't checked. It is not a server-side validation. `sync --dry-run` is different: it still pulls the source workspace and overwrites local files, and only skips the destination.",
		"Confirmation prompts (commit, `push --commit`, `sync`, `workflow disable`) only appear when stdin is a TTY, and read a whole line: answer `n` or `y` followed by Enter. In non-interactive shells (CI, agents) these commands proceed immediately without asking, even without `--force`, so check the target with `suprsend whoami --check` first.",
		"Workflow and template pull and push keep `.suprsend-state.json` in the asset directory (commit it with the files): per workspace, what each item looked like at the last pull or push. Push sends only what changed locally, skips what changed only in the workspace (a stale copy never overwrites a dashboard edit), and fails on items changed on both sides (code `api-conflict`); `--overwrite` pushes the local copy anyway. The CLI ignores every file and directory whose name starts with a dot when reading asset directories.",
		"Committing when the draft already matches live is not an error: `commit`, `push --commit` and `sync` report `unchanged` and exit 0, so re-running them is safe.",
		"Requests are retried up to twice when the connection drops or the API answers 429, 502, 503 or 504. If a commit loses its connection on every attempt, the error says the commit status is unknown; run the same command again, and it reports `unchanged` if the commit went through.",
		"`sync` pushes **and commits** every synced asset in the destination (default `--to production`), so the changes go live immediately.",
		"To give an AI tool direct access to SuprSend, use the hosted MCP server at `https://mcp.suprsend.com/mcp` (sign in with a SuprSend account; for Claude Code: `claude mcp add --transport http suprsend https://mcp.suprsend.com/mcp`) or the `suprsend/claude-plugin` / `suprsend/agent-plugin` plugins. The CLI no longer includes an MCP server: `start-mcp-server` has been removed.",
		"The `profile` command and its subcommands (add, list, modify, remove, use) are only needed for self-hosted/BYOC SuprSend instances, managing multiple accounts, or setting a default workspace (`profile modify --name <p> --workspace <ws>`). SaaS users do not need them. To switch between workspaces within the same account, use the `--workspace` flag or `SUPRSEND_WORKSPACE`.",
	},
}

// generateSkills writes the skill to <dir>/<skillsConfig.Name>/ (SKILL.md plus
// one references/<command>.md page per visible command). GenSkillsDir only
// creates and overwrites files, so the references directory is cleared first;
// otherwise pages for removed or renamed commands would linger. Hidden
// commands (gendocs, genskills) are left out by the generator.
func generateSkills(dir string) error {
	if err := os.MkdirAll(dir, 0o755); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	if err := os.RemoveAll(filepath.Join(dir, skillsConfig.Name, "references")); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	return doc.GenSkillsDir(rootCmd, dir, skillsConfig)
}

var genSkillsCmd = &cobra.Command{
	Use:    "genskills [dir]",
	Hidden: true,
	Short:  "Generate the agent skill (SKILL.md and references)",
	Args:   cobra.ExactArgs(1),
	RunE: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {
		return generateSkills(args[0])
	},
}

func init() {
	genSkillsCmd.SetHelpFunc(func(command *cobra.Command, strings []string) {
		command.Flags().MarkHidden("workspace")
		command.Flags().MarkHidden("service-token")
		command.Flags().MarkHidden("output")
		command.Flags().MarkHidden("verbosity")
		command.Flags().MarkHidden("no-color")
		command.Flags().MarkHidden("config")
		command.Parent().HelpFunc()(command, strings)
	})

	rootCmd.AddCommand(genSkillsCmd)
}
